-## Why NectarLink
+## About this fork
 
-NectarLink came out of my own frustration. I kept juggling Phone Link for
-notifications and messages, KDE Connect for the clipboard and LocalSend for
-files, and always wanted one app that did all of it. So I made one.
+ZoopSync keeps everything the original NectarLink does and changes a few things:
 
-It covers what those three did for me, with one app on each side, plus a lot
-of new features I wanted that I think you'll enjoy having too.
+- **Connect from anywhere** ("Away mode") is on by default, so paired devices stay
+  connected over mobile data and other networks, not just the same Wi-Fi.
+- A new name and icon, and its own app ID, so it installs next to the original.
+- Updates come from this repository's releases, not the original's.
 
